WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.034 --> 00:00:09.634
Are you ready for the Word of God? That's very nice, because we really have a lot of text

2
00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:23.154
to discuss with each other. It is again about a topic that I want to share today and what I want

3
00:00:23.154 --> 00:00:30.674
to discuss regarding something that many Christians who have been walking with Jesus for a long time. For some

4
00:00:30.674 --> 00:00:37.994
people, this is something you have been dealing with for years and what might even be a no-brainer,

5
00:00:37.994 --> 00:00:45.714
but especially when you have been walking with God for a long time and something starts to become a no-brainer, it is sometimes

6
00:00:45.714 --> 00:00:52.234
good to talk about it properly together, because a no-brainer means you do it

7
00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:59.514
simply because you know you do it, because it has become a habit, but sometimes when something

8
00:00:59.514 --> 00:01:09.434
becomes a habit, do you still know what you are doing? Do you understand what I mean? And I consider it

9
00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:16.394
always as a piece of enthusiasm that is within me, that I want to discuss regularly. Various

10
00:01:16.394 --> 00:01:22.794
topics of our Christian faith that I want to explain to those who have only recently believed in

11
00:01:22.794 --> 00:01:31.074
Jesus and want to refresh or maybe even slightly adjust for those who

12
00:01:31.074 --> 00:01:38.994
have believed in Jesus for a long time. Today I want to talk about the topic of speaking in the language of the spirit.

13
00:01:39.954 --> 00:01:47.954
Today I want to talk about praying in tongues, as we say in old Dutch. Personally, I

14
00:01:47.954 --> 00:01:56.634
prefer to call it the languages of the spirit, because tongues, a tongue is simply a language, a tongue setting is

15
00:01:56.634 --> 00:02:06.434
simply a language speech, so tongues I find a bit, I don't say that often, so I say it

16
00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:14.034
preferably just the languages of the spirit. And I would like to talk about that together, because I understand

17
00:02:14.034 --> 00:02:23.074
what kind of church we find ourselves in. This is a church that believes in Father, Son, and Holy Spirit.

18
00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:30.674
We all believe in Father the Creator, in the Son who was obedient to the Father to become

19
00:02:30.794 --> 00:02:37.274
man from God, fully God, fully man in a human body to show humanity

20
00:02:37.274 --> 00:02:42.954
the glory of God. Actually, Jesus came to earth for only one reason and that is to magnify God.

21
00:02:42.954 --> 00:02:48.794
to achieve, that was his goal. And by making God great, he was an example. I believe

22
00:02:48.794 --> 00:02:54.714
namely always in lead by example instead of lead by delegation. You can tell people you

23
00:02:54.714 --> 00:02:59.674
must do this and you must do that and you must do this, or what Jesus did, he did it for

24
00:02:59.674 --> 00:03:05.634
the people. That is what Jesus the Son of God came to do. And I believe in the Holy Spirit. I believe

25
00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:12.834
in the third person of God. He who came to dwell in people. Because of the sin of man

26
00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:20.034
there was distance between God and man, but through the redeeming blood of King Jesus, there is

27
00:03:20.034 --> 00:03:26.354
restoration made that man can live in intimacy with God again. And that intimacy is

28
00:03:26.354 --> 00:03:31.594
even so intimate that the Holy Spirit, through the miraculous blood of the Lamb, has

29
00:03:31.594 --> 00:03:36.474
us cleansed from within and our heart has become a beautiful dwelling place for the Holy Spirit.

30
00:03:36.474 --> 00:03:46.634
Can we say glory, hallelujah, amen or something for the Holy Spirit? Praise God. And I also believe

31
00:03:46.674 --> 00:03:56.114
in the work of the Holy Spirit. This church is a church that believes in the coming of the Holy Spirit.

32
00:03:56.114 --> 00:04:03.314
And I also intentionally say that this is a church that believes in the work of the Holy Spirit. Why

33
00:04:03.314 --> 00:04:09.154
do I say that? You can see these things, worldwide you see different interpretations. And I always proclaim it

34
00:04:09.154 --> 00:04:16.034
over Open Church. Be careful with what you watch on social media. When it comes to the

35
00:04:16.034 --> 00:04:21.274
interpretations of Scripture. Because many people just shout whatever. And I also encounter so much

36
00:04:21.274 --> 00:04:27.274
false teaching on the web. Of which I think, yes it looks very Christian and it can

37
00:04:27.274 --> 00:04:33.194
maybe be a large hall, but that is no indication of the pure Word of God. What

38
00:04:33.194 --> 00:04:40.634
I want to do, what I want to do, is read the Bible together. And let the Bible prove itself.

39
00:04:41.194 --> 00:04:46.274
And especially when we sit with a few hundred people in a hall, and we are going to look at quite a few

40
00:04:46.274 --> 00:04:53.154
verses shortly, then I say, just look, here it says. Because I believe that if we as a church

41
00:04:53.154 --> 00:05:00.914
too little going through Scripture itself, and you have a lot of talking, talking, talking, then people are

42
00:05:00.914 --> 00:05:08.034
very under-informed about what Scripture says. Let us preachers say a little less. And I

43
00:05:08.034 --> 00:05:13.634
am speaking here to Tim Lauree, a big man with a lot of talk, but let us preachers say less

44
00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:24.674
and read more from God's Word. Amen? All right. Speaking in the languages of the Spirit.

45
00:05:26.554 --> 00:05:34.834
Maybe you come to this church as a newcomer and sometimes hear someone praying in the languages of

46
00:05:34.874 --> 00:05:46.074
the Spirit. And then you think to yourself, what is that? What then? What? I don't understand that. You are baptized

47
00:05:46.074 --> 00:05:53.074
in baptismal water, you come up from the baptismal water, and we always pray then, we lay our hand on the

48
00:05:53.074 --> 00:06:00.234
heart or on the shoulder of a young lady, and then we pray that God will give His Spirit a filling

49
00:06:00.234 --> 00:06:05.994
in the life of the new Christian. Why is this important? Because you need to know

50
00:06:05.994 --> 00:06:13.474
that you know, that you know, that you know that God's Spirit is in you. For if God's Spirit is in you,

51
00:06:13.474 --> 00:06:19.514
He will never let you rest again. And as a beautiful gift, God is faithful. If we are not

52
00:06:19.514 --> 00:06:24.674
faithful to Him, He is still faithful to us. For the righteous will fall, but by the

53
00:06:24.674 --> 00:06:30.994
power of the Holy Spirit we will rise in the grace of the Lord. So beautiful, so important

54
00:06:30.994 --> 00:06:37.634
that you need the Holy Spirit in your heart. But then there is often prayer, we pray

55
00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:50.754
that you will also learn to pray in the language of the Spirit. And then you think, wow, what is that? And I believe that this

56
00:06:50.754 --> 00:06:58.434
is still a gift of the Holy Spirit today. I speak in the languages of the Holy Spirit,

57
00:06:58.434 --> 00:07:04.354
but I am not going to prove it to you now, because I am going to tell you some things about it shortly.

58
00:07:04.354 --> 00:07:09.514
About a small adjustment that we might need to make in the church. Maybe a small,

59
00:07:09.514 --> 00:07:17.474
I think we are doing 99% well, but I just want to indicate a refreshment about what we

60
00:07:17.474 --> 00:07:25.394
are actually doing when we pray in the languages of the Spirit. Now, the Holy Spirit is

61
00:07:25.394 --> 00:07:33.394
spirit. You do not see where it is. It is just like the wind. You feel it, you notice it, but you do not see it

62
00:07:33.394 --> 00:07:39.234
no, you cannot grasp it either. But the Holy Spirit does wonderful things. He can raise people

63
00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:45.794
from the grave. He can give people insights about things you never knew about yourself

64
00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:52.754
that you would be so wise. Sometimes you can say things. Jesus who promises and says to his disciples

65
00:07:52.754 --> 00:07:59.994
when you are later brought before a council because of my name and you are almost crucified or

66
00:07:59.994 --> 00:08:06.714
stoned for the name of all names, his name is King Jesus, do not be afraid of what you will say,

67
00:08:06.714 --> 00:08:13.754
for the Holy Spirit will give you words that you did not even know you were so smart.

68
00:08:13.754 --> 00:08:17.874
And I have experienced this myself, I am not a smart guy at all, but sometimes I have told things

69
00:08:17.874 --> 00:08:24.714
to people that I thought, that is wise man. That is really smart. And I have heard this from several people

70
00:08:24.714 --> 00:08:33.474
in testimonies, that God can give us things, words of wisdom and words of knowledge.

71
00:08:33.474 --> 00:08:40.594
And God can do things in us that are supernatural, that go beyond our own nature,

72
00:08:40.594 --> 00:08:49.514
that go beyond our intelligence quotient, that are supernatural and those things are deeper and broader

73
00:08:49.514 --> 00:09:00.434
and more beautiful and more powerful and more inhuman, for we are talking about God and not about human rational thinking. Amen.

74
00:09:00.434 --> 00:09:05.914
All right. We all know this, we will read quickly, for I just said that we would read a lot.

75
00:09:05.954 --> 00:09:09.474
Acts chapter 2, verses 1 to 13 we will read quickly.

76
00:09:09.474 --> 00:09:13.554
If you have your Bible, I encourage you to go to your own Bible.

77
00:09:13.554 --> 00:09:20.674
If you happen to have a pen or a highlighter at hand, always take notes or grab a notebook.

78
00:09:20.674 --> 00:09:29.114
But I want to motivate us, have your own Bible. Read your Bible and pray every day if you want to grow. Amen.

79
00:09:29.114 --> 00:09:35.314
Okay, Acts chapter 2. If you are there, say Amen.

80
00:09:35.314 --> 00:09:38.634
That is good. Acts chapter 2, verse 1.

81
00:09:38.634 --> 00:09:43.994
We see here the coming of the Holy Spirit upon all people.

82
00:09:43.994 --> 00:09:53.594
Small note, I sometimes hear online that, I heard someone say this week, that David would be jealous of us,

83
00:09:53.594 --> 00:09:58.274
because David would say, what you have, I have never had, the Holy Spirit.

84
00:09:58.274 --> 00:10:01.034
I'm not so sure about all that.

85
00:10:01.034 --> 00:10:08.034
I believe that the Holy Spirit, the Ruach of God, the Spirit of God, has always been present.

86
00:10:08.034 --> 00:10:16.954
Only through the sins of man and through the Israelites did sacrifices need to be made to regain atonement for their sins.

87
00:10:16.954 --> 00:10:23.874
And that was a process that could not continue, because it was not complete in the cleansing.

88
00:10:23.914 --> 00:10:31.034
It needed the blood of the lamb, Jesus Christ. He is the true lamb who died for all people.

89
00:10:31.034 --> 00:10:35.114
But that does not mean that God's spirit was not present among His people.

90
00:10:35.114 --> 00:10:40.394
There were indeed prophets and people of God who truly had the fulfillment of the Holy Spirit.

91
00:10:40.394 --> 00:10:46.794
This is also said about Samson, this is said about various judges, this is said about various prophets,

92
00:10:46.794 --> 00:10:50.634
that they were filled with the Holy Spirit and could do certain things.

93
00:10:50.674 --> 00:11:00.474
The big difference is, through the blood of Jesus, the Holy Spirit has come upon all people.

94
00:11:00.474 --> 00:11:02.274
And that is a big difference.

95
00:11:02.274 --> 00:11:08.874
Because now you no longer have to come to the church to look at a holy man on a stage who is filled with the Holy Spirit.

96
00:11:08.874 --> 00:11:13.434
Now you come to the church as the temple of the Holy Spirit yourself.

97
00:11:13.434 --> 00:11:16.434
And we are together temples of the Holy Spirit.

98
00:11:16.474 --> 00:11:22.034
And that is groundbreaking for what Jesus has done and the coming of the Holy Spirit.

99
00:11:22.034 --> 00:11:29.634
So what we read here in Acts chapter 2 is the coming of the Holy Spirit and the outpouring of the Holy Spirit.

100
00:11:29.634 --> 00:11:38.114
You could say, first it was a priest or a prophet or a judge and now it is the outpouring upon all.

101
00:11:38.114 --> 00:11:42.034
We read this here in Acts chapter 2 verse 1.

102
00:11:42.634 --> 00:11:48.714
On Pentecost, they were all together.

103
00:11:48.714 --> 00:11:54.594
Suddenly there was a sound like a violent wind blowing through the whole house.

104
00:11:54.594 --> 00:11:57.674
And there were what looked like flames of fire.

105
00:11:57.674 --> 00:12:03.834
That fire divided and came upon them, we all say, all of us, hallelujah.

106
00:12:03.874 --> 00:12:12.114
And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in other tongues.

107
00:12:12.114 --> 00:12:14.714
These were languages that the Spirit of God gave them.

108
00:12:15.914 --> 00:12:18.114
So what are the languages of the Spirit?

109
00:12:18.114 --> 00:12:23.634
It is a gift that God gives.

110
00:12:23.634 --> 00:12:31.434
Not done by oneself, not practiced by oneself, not trying to cook it up by oneself,

111
00:12:31.434 --> 00:12:38.034
not doing it because you come to a church where you hear people praying in the languages of the Spirit

112
00:12:38.034 --> 00:12:43.434
and then engaging in some sort of mirror-neuronal behavior,

113
00:12:43.434 --> 00:12:50.834
not practicing by yourself and doing your best, it is something that the Holy Spirit gives you.

114
00:12:50.834 --> 00:12:56.314
Underline, these were languages that the Spirit of God gave them.

115
00:12:56.314 --> 00:13:00.514
In Jerusalem lived religious Jews from all nations of the world.

116
00:13:00.514 --> 00:13:03.514
When they heard the sound, they all came to see.

117
00:13:03.514 --> 00:13:12.314
They were truly amazed, for everyone from all those different nations heard the twelve apostles speaking in their own language.

118
00:13:12.314 --> 00:13:16.314
Look, a miracle of languages is taking place.

119
00:13:16.314 --> 00:13:22.314
Astonished, they said, aren't those men all Galileans?

120
00:13:22.314 --> 00:13:26.314
How is it then that we hear them speaking in our own language?

121
00:13:26.314 --> 00:13:43.314
For we are here with partners and with companions and elements, residents of Mesopotamia, Judea, Cappadocia, Pontus, Asia, Phrygia, Pamphylia, Egypt and the regions of Libya near Cyrene, Romans, Cretans, Jews and people who have converted to the Jewish faith.

122
00:13:43.314 --> 00:13:53.314
Cretans and even Arabs, and we hear them all telling about the wonderful things God has done in our own language.

123
00:13:53.314 --> 00:13:57.314
They were utterly amazed.

124
00:13:57.314 --> 00:14:02.314
They did not know what to think, they said to each other, what is going on here?

125
00:14:02.314 --> 00:14:08.314
Verse 13, but others said mockingly, they have had too much to drink.

126
00:14:08.314 --> 00:14:16.314
Look, here is an interpretation from Tim Lauré, which I actually never hear around me.

127
00:14:16.314 --> 00:14:20.314
So do with it what you will.

128
00:14:20.314 --> 00:14:25.314
Look closely at what you see happening here.

129
00:14:25.314 --> 00:14:33.314
You see that God's spirit gives fluent speech, another language.

130
00:14:33.314 --> 00:14:41.314
So you suddenly arrive in Jerusalem, knowing that the people speak Hebrew or Aramaic or whatever in that language, at that time.

131
00:14:41.314 --> 00:14:54.314
And you come there as a Dutch person and you hear it fluently in your accent and in your language.

132
00:14:54.314 --> 00:15:01.314
That someone is proclaiming, there has been a distance caused by your sin.

133
00:15:01.314 --> 00:15:07.314
And because of your sin, there has been no time when you could live in relationship with God.

134
00:15:07.314 --> 00:15:10.314
But praise King Jesus, He has come.

135
00:15:10.314 --> 00:15:13.314
Jesus of Nazareth has come, He was God.

136
00:15:13.314 --> 00:15:16.314
He became man, He died on a cross.

137
00:15:16.314 --> 00:15:18.314
He has risen from the grave.

138
00:15:18.314 --> 00:15:21.314
Jesus is here, here is the good news.

139
00:15:21.314 --> 00:15:24.314
I know who you are, I know what you have done.

140
00:15:24.314 --> 00:15:27.314
He might even call you almost by name, for I was not there.

141
00:15:27.314 --> 00:15:34.314
But it was so finely tuned that in their own language they heard the love and the good news.

142
00:15:34.314 --> 00:15:40.314
In the gospel, the good news explained in their own language.

143
00:15:40.314 --> 00:15:48.314
Wonderful, thank you dear king for this language miracle.

144
00:15:48.314 --> 00:15:59.314
What went wrong in the tower of Babel due to unity against God, where God said I will spread the language at this moment.

145
00:15:59.314 --> 00:16:07.314
Through the coming of King Jesus and the coming of the Holy Spirit, God has brought the nations together again in one name.

146
00:16:07.314 --> 00:16:09.314
And that name is Jesus.

147
00:16:09.314 --> 00:16:14.314
So God has brought restoration from Babel, poof, across the world.

148
00:16:14.314 --> 00:16:17.314
It literally says and there was confusion.

149
00:16:17.314 --> 00:16:22.314
And with the coming of the New Church in the name of Jesus, there comes restoration.

150
00:16:22.314 --> 00:16:25.314
And He brings all languages under King Jesus again.

151
00:16:25.314 --> 00:16:27.314
And He brings it as a language miracle.

152
00:16:27.314 --> 00:16:32.314
And I am sure that the readers of Acts understood that this was happening.

153
00:16:32.314 --> 00:16:43.314
However, there are Christians who say yes but that happened then and that was only then and so that is not happening now.

154
00:16:43.314 --> 00:16:45.314
But that is a wrong way of thinking.

155
00:16:46.314 --> 00:16:55.314
Because what I hear many people say is that speaking in the language of the Spirit, what they hear from Christians, is just nonsense.

156
00:16:55.314 --> 00:16:59.314
It's just gibberish, it's just nonsense and we all don't do that because that's nonsense.

157
00:16:59.314 --> 00:17:01.314
But here is my explanation.

158
00:17:01.314 --> 00:17:03.314
For example, if you look at verse 13.

159
00:17:03.314 --> 00:17:08.314
But other people said mockingly they have just drunk too much.

160
00:17:08.314 --> 00:17:22.314
I am one hundred percent sure that if you hear the gospel spoken in your perfect language, you would also be amazed and would never say they are just drunk.

161
00:17:22.314 --> 00:17:32.314
What I interpret here and what I see happening is that it is through the faith that is in those people or the unbelief in those people.

162
00:17:32.314 --> 00:17:46.314
If you had approached that situation with an unbelieving heart, you would have just heard the tongue language, perhaps the gibberish that you do not understand, and you would have said those people are totally crazy.

163
00:17:46.314 --> 00:17:57.314
But if you come to God with a believing heart, a worshiping heart, and thus receive the interpretation from the Holy Spirit, you hear the good news.

164
00:17:57.314 --> 00:18:01.314
Through that same language, you can praise and worship God for it.

165
00:18:01.314 --> 00:18:03.314
Do you understand my distinction?

166
00:18:03.314 --> 00:18:08.314
So God does one work and you have two different reactions.

167
00:18:08.314 --> 00:18:10.314
How is that? It comes from your heart.

168
00:18:13.314 --> 00:18:22.314
And so what God does through the tongues of the Spirit is what God wants to do through the tongues of the Spirit.

169
00:18:22.314 --> 00:18:28.314
It is His Spirit, it is His language, it is His way of working.

170
00:18:28.314 --> 00:18:34.314
Whatever you think about it or whatever you do not think about it, that is actually not up to God.

171
00:18:34.314 --> 00:18:45.314
For God says if I choose to spit on the ground, make mud, and smear someone's eyes so that he can see again.

172
00:18:45.314 --> 00:18:50.314
Then God must know for Himself that He makes mud and spits in someone's eyes.

173
00:18:50.314 --> 00:18:55.314
And people can then say to themselves, I find that strange, why do you have to spit in his eyes?

174
00:18:55.314 --> 00:18:59.314
Do you know what that blind man who could see again gives for that?

175
00:18:59.314 --> 00:19:04.314
Absolutely nothing, spit away as long as I can see again.

176
00:19:04.314 --> 00:19:09.314
And so it is about your heart attitude towards the works of God.

177
00:19:09.314 --> 00:19:14.314
God loves to do strange things.

178
00:19:14.314 --> 00:19:22.314
Do you know why? Because through the strangeness of God, my thoughts are not your thoughts.

179
00:19:22.314 --> 00:19:25.314
My ways are not your ways.

180
00:19:25.314 --> 00:19:30.314
He says to a widow with just a little flour and a little oil, give me that.

181
00:19:30.314 --> 00:19:36.314
Then you might die later. No, give me that so I can provide.

182
00:19:36.314 --> 00:19:40.314
God is supernatural.

183
00:19:40.314 --> 00:19:43.314
He walks on water when He wants to walk on water.

184
00:19:43.314 --> 00:19:46.314
He splits seas when He wants to split seas.

185
00:19:46.314 --> 00:19:53.314
He also goes through a people with a death angel when it pleases Him in His will.

186
00:19:53.314 --> 00:19:57.314
And He speaks in the language of the Spirit as much as He wants.

187
00:19:57.314 --> 00:20:03.314
And we humans have only one thing to do, to have a heart attitude of receptiveness.

188
00:20:03.314 --> 00:20:08.314
And so when people say, oh yes, speaking in tongues or speaking in the languages of the Spirit,

189
00:20:08.314 --> 00:20:11.314
it's just what happens there in Acts chapter 2.

190
00:20:11.314 --> 00:20:15.314
And every time I hear people, the critics, I hear them say that too.

191
00:20:15.314 --> 00:20:19.314
Yes, that was only Acts chapter 2 and that was only for the spreading of the gospel.

192
00:20:19.314 --> 00:20:21.314
And then I think, no way.

193
00:20:21.314 --> 00:20:25.314
Because then you are not reading Scripture, because there is so much more to tell about that.

194
00:20:25.314 --> 00:20:28.314
Right? All right.

195
00:20:28.314 --> 00:20:38.314
So what is really cool about that Acts situation, what is truly brilliant of God, of what He did there,

196
00:20:38.314 --> 00:20:45.314
is that all kinds of people from all over the world come on a pilgrimage to Jerusalem,

197
00:20:45.314 --> 00:20:50.314
for the Pentecost, yes, and they come there to worship God.

198
00:20:50.314 --> 00:21:03.314
Jesus has risen, the Holy Spirit comes, and the Holy Spirit gives a nuclear bomb of His power and His goodness.

199
00:21:03.314 --> 00:21:05.314
Boom, at that moment.

200
00:21:05.314 --> 00:21:10.314
And He gives the gospel, the language miracle was actually what really happens there.

201
00:21:10.314 --> 00:21:14.314
The language miracle is not necessarily that you hear someone speaking your own language...

